ge.\n\n**Candidates 0, 3, 6, 7** follow one every-two-days pattern at different sizes. Candidate 7 (good 1 at about 1.15× forecast, good 0 at about 1.09×) looks like the best of them. Candidate 0 overbuys good 1 (1.25×) and underbuys good 0 (1.0×), and comes out about even with candidate 7.\n\n**Candidate 1 compared with candidate 7:**\n- **Fixed charge:** 10 order days instead of 14 saves about 148.\n- **Shortages:** candidate 1 orders good 1 at about 1.11× forecast per 3-day cycle. Over three days the random swings partly cancel, so the expected shortfall per day comes out almost the same as candidate 7's 1.155× on 2-day cycles.\n- **Purchases:** candidate 1 buys 30 fewer units of good 1 (about +120) and 15 fewer of good 0 (about +135). The leaner good-0 stock may cost about 60 in extra missed sales.\n- **Holding:** longer cycles mean more stock sitting on the shelf, costing about 130 for good 1 and about 50 for good 0.\n- **Net:** candidate 1 comes out roughly 100–160 ahead.\n\n**Robustness:** good 1 lasts 4 days and each candidate-1 batch covers 3, so any leftover still sells on the first day of the next cycle. Its quantities follow the forecast evenly (about 1.05–1.11× in every cycle), so no single day's swing exposes it more than the others."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3785, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3785}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:41:26.709Z", "request_id": "req_011CgB8vb915KBXUcgoDFLeW"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_