\n| 4 | 14 | ≈1.00 | same as 7 | Item 0 ordered every 4 days: less stock and more storage cost than 7 |\n| 1 | 10 | ≈1.01 | ≈1.065 | See below |\n| 2 | 10 | — | — | Large item 0 deliveries every 6 days; around day 11 the 200-unit limit is exceeded and stock is lost |\n\n**Candidate 7 against candidate 1**\n- Candidate 1 orders every 3 days, so it pays 4 fewer order fees: +148.\n- Its stock stays on the shelf longer. Extra storage is about 4.6 per day for item 1 and about 1.7 per day for item 0, roughly −175 in total.\n- It buys less: about 15 fewer units of item 0 (about −50 in shortages) and about 30 fewer of item 1 (about −75).\n- Net, candidate 7 comes out ahead by roughly 150.\n\n**If demand moves away from forecast:** candidate 7 has a moderate buffer on both items. Its short 2-day cycles let leftover stock carry into the next delivery period. Candidates 0 and 6 get hit by high-demand days, and candidate 3 is hurt by spoilage when demand is low. That makes 7 the most stable."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 360, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 360}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:42:51.178Z", "request_id": "req_011CgB94EXVKizbFt8eLWAqn"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012DQgDv5f7tuGaT5TxEEAMf", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_01