Candidate 7 has about the same product 1 costs as candidate 1, but pays 148 more in fixed costs.\n\n3. **Product 0 (lasts 8 days) is also fine in candidate 1.** It orders about 6% above forecast every three days, close to the true average demand. The long shelf life smooths out the swings.\n   - Candidate 2 has the same order days but buys product 0 in six-day batches. That means higher holding costs, slightly too little in total, and the warehouse overflowing around day 11.\n   - Candidate 4 orders product 0 in four-day lumps and still pays the two-day fixed cost.\n\n4. **On risk,** the three-day cycle fits product 1's 4-day shelf life well. Candidate 1's small, steady safety margin keeps it stable when actual demand differs from the forecast. Its main rival is candidate 7, whose costs other than the fixed fee are about equal.\n\nI put the probability that candidate 1 is actually best at 0.6."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3832, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3832}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:46:09.788Z", "request_id": "req_011CgB9FXPZHJmCUCv7ALgMy"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XzApuTsFM9u2EkPGfUb1X2", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgB9FXoNWwDxC2hiB9Cah", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": 